THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL

The grant above covers the Adjustments Builder application and the adjustment
library. It does not extend to third-party material referenced by the app.

The curriculum feature stores learning-area names, level names and code prefixes
so that a school can link an adjustment to its own curriculum. Where those names
are Victorian Curriculum F-10 naming conventions, they are used as reference
labels only:

  The Victorian Curriculum F-10 content elements are (c) VCAA, licensed
  CC-BY-NC. The Victorian Curriculum F-10 and related content can be accessed
  directly at the VCAA website (https://f10.vcaa.vic.edu.au).

No Victorian Curriculum content descriptions, elaborations or achievement
standards are included in or distributed with this application. Where a user
pastes curriculum text into their own plan, that text stays on their device and
remains subject to the licence of whoever published it. Complying with that
licence is the user's responsibility, not the author's.

NOTICE

The adjustment library distributed with this application is a working draft. It
was assembled in one school and expanded with AI assistance. It is not
departmental policy, not approved guidance, and not a substitute for
professional judgement or your school's own processes. Every adjustment it
produces is a starting point that a person must check before it is agreed or
acted upon.
